proof.text:
Set $b=c_h\circ L_h(c_k):L'A_X\to A_Z$. Its adjunct under the composite adjunction is $R'(b)\eta'_{A_X}$ [def-weil-pbc-composite-adjunction]. Using functoriality and naturality of the unit $\eta_h$ at $c_k:L_kA_X\to A_Y$, compute
$$\begin{aligned}
R'(b)\eta'_{A_X}
&=R_k\bigl(R_h(c_h)R_hL_h(c_k)\eta_{h,L_kA_X}\bigr)\eta_{k,A_X}\\
&=R_k\bigl(R_h(c_h)\eta_{h,A_Y}c_k\bigr)\eta_{k,A_X}\\
&=R_k(\rho^h)R_k(c_k)\eta_{k,A_X}
=R_k(\rho^h)\rho^k.
\end{aligned}$$
The last line uses $R_f(c_f)\eta_{f,A_{\mathrm{target}(f)}}=\rho^f$, exactly the fact that $c_f$ is adjunct to $\rho^f$ in [def-weil-proetale-inverse-image]. Every expression is a map of ring sheaves.

The adjunct under $L\dashv R$ of $b\alpha_{A_X}$ is $R(b\alpha_{A_X})\eta_{kh,A_X}$ [def-weil-proetale-inverse-image]. Compose this adjunct with $d_{A_Z}$, use naturality of $d$ at $b$, then Step 3's unit equation, Step 4 and Step 2:
$$\begin{aligned}
d_{A_Z}R(b\alpha_{A_X})\eta_{kh,A_X}
&=R'(b)d_{L'A_X}R(\alpha_{A_X})\eta_{kh,A_X}\\
&=R'(b)\eta'_{A_X}
=R_k(\rho^h)\rho^k
=d_{A_Z}\rho^{kh}.
\end{aligned}$$
Cancel the isomorphism $d_{A_Z}$. The adjunction is a bijection on ring-sheaf morphisms, so its injectivity identifies $b\alpha_{A_X}$ with the map whose adjunct is $\rho^{kh}$, namely $c_{kh}$. Substituting $b=c_hh^{-1}(c_k)$ gives exactly the displayed equality of the item.
